2 CONT
2 CONT Parents
2 CONT  	 Father: Robert II DE SARREBRUCK-COMMERCY, comte de Roucy (1492-1504) seigneur de Braine et de Commercy
2 CONT
2 CONT  	 Mother: Marie D'AMBOISE, dame de Ricey 
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippine_de_Sarrebruck-Commercy
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippine de Sarrebruck-Commercy, (1490 - Montmirail on June 8, 1551), lord of Commercy-Château-Haut, viscountess of Louvois, lady of Montmirail, is the daughter of Robert II of Sarrebruck-Commercy and Marie d'Amboise, she - same
2 CONC  daughter of Charles I of Amboise. After the death of her husband in 1516 she continued to reside at the castle of La Roche-Guyon where she learned of the death of her brother Amé III in 1525 and thereby inherited the rich lordshi
2 CONC p of Commercy. From then on she took the title of "Damoiselle de Commercy, Lord of Montmirail and Souldron, Baroness and Viscountess of Loupvois, Lady of Germenes and Cocey". He took possession of Commercy on November 17, 1526 whe
2 CONC n his squire Guillaume Bouchet presented himself at the castle and received the oath of loyalty from Governor Jean de Dommartin. She wrote her will on June 7, 1551 and chose to be buried at the Château de Montmirail1
2 CONT
2 CONT She married in 1504, at the age of fourteen, Charles de Silly, (1475/77 - August 4, 1516/18), Lord of Rochefort-en-Yvelines, from whom she was1:
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicolas, died in Asti on October 4, 1527, Louis, (? - before 1565), count of La Roche-Guyon, he married on February 16, 1539 Anne de Laval, (Château de Comper on June 29, 1525 - after 1572), from whom he had Henri, Antoine, and Ca
2 CONC therine married November 25 / December 1565 to François Chabot, Jacques, (? - 1570), count of La Rochepot, lord of La Roche Guyon and Montmirail, he married Marie Madeleine d'Annebault, (1541 - June 3, 1568), Catherine, she marrie
2 CONC d on March 25, 1536 François de Rohan, (1515 - 1559), Lord of Gié, Viscount of Fronsac and Count of Orbec, son of Charles de Rohan-Gié.
