1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Louis IV de Bueil, Comte de Sancerre (died c. 1565) was the Count of Sancerre from 1537 until his death. Great cup-bearer of the king of France, Knight of the Order of King, Count of Sancerre (1537-1563), governor 
2 CONC of Anjou, Touraine and Maine . He commanded the French defenders during the Siege of St. Dizier (1544). He fought at Battle of Marignano, Battle of Pavia, Battle of St. Quentin (1557) . https://www.revolvy.com/main/index.php?s=Lou
2 CONC is+IV+de+Bueil%2C+Comte+de+Sancerre&item_type=topic
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis IV de Bueil, Comte de Sancerre From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to: navigation, search  Louis IV de Bueil, Comte de Sancerre (died c. 1565) was the Count of Sancerre from 1537 until his death. Great cup-bearer of the king of France, Knight of the Order of King, Count of Sancerre (1537-156
2 CONC 3), governor of Anjou, Touraine and Maine . He commanded the French defenders during the Siege of St. Dizier (1544). He fought at Battle of Marignano, Battle of Pavia, Battle of St. Quentin (1557) .
2 CONT
