1 NAME François /de Vergy/
2 GIVN François
2 SURN de Vergy
2 _MARNM de Vergy
1 NAME François de Vergy, comte de Champlitte
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1530
1 DEAT
2 DATE 5 DEC 1591
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00112239&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY François de Vergy, comte de Champlitte, was born in 1530, the son of Guillaume V de Vergy, seigneur de Montferrand, d'Autrey et Champlitte, and Marine bâtarde de Bourgogne. His mother was the natural daughter of Baudouin
2 CONC  de Bourgogne, sire de Falais, himself the natural son of Philippe 'the Good', duc de Bourgogne.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the Schmalkaldic War (1546-47), fought between the Habsburgs and the Schmalkaldic League of the empire's Protestant territories, François had his first experience of warfare as a page at the Battle of Neuburg in Bavaria in 
2 CONC July 1546, close to Maximilian II, the future son-in-law of Emperor Charles V. Rewarded for his courage, he had the honour of carrying Maximilian's standard at the Battle of Mühlberg on 24 April 1547, a victory of the Habsburgs ov
2 CONC er the Schmalkaldic League.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 13 June 1553, François married his cousin Claudine de Pontailler, daughter of Henri de Pontailler, seigneur de Flagey, and Antoinette de Vergy, dame de Fouvent, the daughter of François' uncle Claude de Vergy. François and Clau
2 CONC dine had four children of whom only their daughter Béatrice would have progeny, marrying Evandelin Simon de Cusance, baron de Belvoir.
2 CONT
2 CONT Claudine died in 1576, and in 1577 François married Renée de Ray, dame de Vaudrey, daughter of Claude de Ray, seigneur de Ray. They had a son Clériadus and daughter Alexandrine, neither of whom would have progeny.
2 CONT
2 CONT François succeeded his uncle Claude de Vergy as governor of the county of Burgundy (Franche-Comté). In 1586 he was made a member of the Order of the Golden Fleece, like his uncle before him.
2 CONT
2 CONT François lived in Dôle, the capital of Franche-Comté, in the city of Gray and in the Vergy château de Champlitte, where he ran what was effectively a court. He rebuilt the Châteaufort in a grander style.
2 CONT
2 CONT François died on 5 December 1591. He was succeeded as governor of Franche-Comté by his son Claude from his first marriage. On Claude's death in 1602 he was succeeded as governor by his half-brother Clériadus.
