2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Early life
2 CONT
2 CONT Portrait of Margaret by Jean Hey, ca. 1490 (aged ten)
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1483, she was betrothed to the Dauphin of France, later King Charles VIII of France, bringing with her a dowry of Franche-Comté and Artois, and was transferred to the guardianship of King Louis XI of France (see Treaty of Arras
2 CONC , 1482). She received a fine education. After Charles renounced the treaty and married Anne, Duchess of Brittany, Margaret was returned to her father in 1493.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Marriages
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan, Prince of Asturias
2 CONT
2 CONT first husband
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Philibert II, Duke of Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT second husband
2 CONT
2 CONT
