1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Louise de Bourbon-Lavedan born on October 21, 1548 and died on January 11, 1637[ 1 ] , [ 2 ] , is the daughter of Jean de Bourbon-Lavedan, Viscount of Lavedan and Françoise de Silly [ 3 ] . Her father was the son o
2 CONC fCharles de Bourbon-Lavedan, who was himself the son ofJean II de Bourbon. She wasabbess of Fontevraudfrom 1611 toJanuary 11, 1637[ 4 ] .
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT First a grand prioress, Louise de Bourbon-Lavedan became Abbess of Fontevraud in 1611 [ 5 ] . In 1618, she created a seminary, the Petit Fontevraud, at La Flèche , for the monks of her priory Saint-Jean de l'Habit [ 6 ] . She also
2 CONC  had this priory enclosed [ 6 ] .
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1626, she wrote the first Ceremonial of the Order of Fontevrault [ 5 ] . In 1632 she built a library for her monastery [ 5 ] , she also restored the Saint Lazare priory within her Abbey . Her abbacy was marked by numerous confl
2 CONC icts with the monks of Saint-Jean de l'Habit, the monks having difficulty accepting the authority of a woman over them [ 5 ] .
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT Patricia M. Gathercole , “  Illustrations of the “Roman de Renart”: Manuscripts BN fr. 1581 and BN fr. 12584  ”, Gesta , vol.  10, no .  1,January 1971, p.  39–44 ( ISSN  0016-920X and 2169-3099 , DOI  10.2307/766567 , read online
2 CONC   [ archive ] , consulted onJune 22, 2024)
2 CONT "  2- History of the order of Fontevraud, its founders, its Abbesses and other administrators.  [ archive ]  ", on Dictionary of the monastic order of Fontevaudre ,May 17, 2011 (consulted onJune 22, 2024)
2 CONT "  Louise de Bourbon de Lavedan | Nuns in pictures  [ archive ]  ", on cercornum.univ-st-etienne.fr (consulted onJune 22, 2024)
2 CONT "  Louise de Bourbon-Lavedan | Nuns in pictures  [ archive ]  ", on cercornum.univ-st-etienne.fr (consulted onJune 22, 2024)
