2 CONT Eleanor of Austria (15 November 1498 – 25 February 1558), also called Eleonor of Castile, was born Archduchess of Austria and Infanta of Castile from the House of Habsburg, and became subsequently in turn Queen consort of Portugal
2 CONC  (1518–1521) and of France. She also held the Duchy of Touraine (1547–1558) as dower. She is called Leonor in Spanish and Portuguese and "Éléonore" or Aliénor in French.
2 CONT
