1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Louise de Rieux'''1
2 CONT Last Edited	13 Dec 2008
2 CONT F, #107635
2 CONT '''Father'''	Claude I de Rieux, 19th Seigneur de Rieux, Rochefort, & Assérac, Comte d'Harcourt & d'Aumale, Baron de Malestroit2 b. 15 May 1497, d. 19 May 1532
2 CONT '''Mother'''	Suzanne de Bourbon2 b. 1508, d. Feb 1570
2 CONT '''     Louise de Rieux married René de Lorraine, Marquis d'Elbeuf, General of the Galleys''', son of Claude I de Lorraine, Duke d'Aumale, Comte de Guise and Antoinette de Bourbon, '''on 3 February 1555.'''1,3
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT '''René de Lorraine, Marquis d'Elbeuf, General of the Galleys''' b. 14 Aug 1536, d. 1566
2 CONT '''Children	'''
2 CONT *Marie of Lorraine+1 b. 22 Aug 1555, d. c 1605
2 CONT *Charles I de Lorraine, Duke d'Elbeuf, Comte d'Harcourt, Lillebonne, & Rieux, Governor of Poitou,+4 b. 18 Oct 1556, d. 24 Aug 1605
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT 1.[S11569] Europaische Stammtafeln, by Wilhelm Karl, Prinz zu Isenburg, Vol. VI, Tafel 134.
2 CONT 2.[S11569] Europaische Stammtafeln, by Wilhelm Karl, Prinz zu Isenburg, Vol. III, Tafel 75.
2 CONT 3.[S2] Detlev Schwennicke, Europaische Stammtafeln, New Series, Vol. I/2, Tafel 209.
2 CONT 4..[S2] Detlev Schwennicke, Europaische Stammtafeln, New Series, Vol. I/2, Tafel 211.
2 CONT From: https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p3584.htm#i107635
2 CONT ____
2 CONT '''Louise d'Harcourt '''
2 CONT F, #42285, b. 1531
2 CONT Last Edited=3 Feb 2004
2 CONT '''     Louise d'Harcourt was born in 1531. She married René de Guise, Duc de Lorraine-Elboeuf,''' son of Claude de Lorraine, Duc de Guise and Antoinette de Bourbon, '''in 1554.'''
2 CONT '''Children of Louise d'Harcourt and René de Guise, Duc de Lorraine-Elboeuf'''
2 CONT 1. Marie de Lorraine b. 1555, d. c 1603
2 CONT 2. Charles I de Lorraine, Duc de Elboeuf+ b. 1556, d. 1605
2 CONT From: https://www.thepeerage.com/p4229.htm#i42285
2 CONT _______
2 CONT '''René II de Lorraine, Marquis d'Elbeuf''' (14 August 1536 – 14 December 1566)[1] was a French noble, and soldier during the latter Italian Wars and early French Wars of Religion. The youngest son of Claude of Lorraine, Duke of G
2 CONC uise and Antoinette of Bourbon-Vendôme Elbeuf's career began at a young age. '''etc.
2 CONT Over the following years he worked with his brothers in the prosecution of their feud with the Admiral, who they blamed for the assassination of the Duke of Guise, participating in their armed entrance into Paris in 1565. The foll
2 CONC owing year he would die in Provence.
2 CONT Early life and family
2 CONT Childhood
2 CONT '''René''' was born at Joinville, Haute-Marne in 1536, the sixth son of Claude, Duke of Guise and Antoinette de Bourbon. Only fourteen years old at the death of his father in 1550. It was agreed that like Claude, Duke of Aumale he
2 CONC  would be established as a Norman lord, receiving the inheritance of the barony of Elbeuf. For now he was too young to rule it and it set aside for him, while he stayed at Joinville under the wardship of his mother.[2] Antoinette 
2 CONC would administer his estates during his youth, and further prosecute the struggle in the Parlement of Paris for the elevation of the barony of Elbeuf into a marquisate.[3]
2 CONT As '''Elbeuf's''' tutor she selected Charles des Boves to replace the recently deceased Etienne de Morainville, who was reputed to have provided his charge with a 'good and wise education'.[4]
2 CONT In return for the privileges he acquired, it was expected that he would be deferential to his older brothers and mother. He allowed his mother to pick the members of his household, meanwhile his gendarmerie company was to be selec
2 CONC ted by his brothers.[5] He was a patron of the arts, particularly of the composer Pierre Clereau of Lorraine. The poet Remy Belleau followed Elbeuf on his campaign into Italy in 1557, and he became the man's patron over the next s
2 CONC everal years until Belleau's conversion to Protestantism in 1560.[6]
2 CONT Marriage and children
2 CONT '''He married Louise de Rieux (1531 – c. 1570) on 3 February 1555. This marriage was considered very impressive for a sixth son, as she was an heiress to a considerable estate. Henri II felt it was improper for a woman of her stat
2 CONC us to marry a baron, and as such raised the barony of Elbeuf to a marquisate. As part of the dowry, Louise brought parts of the County of Harcourt making him a powerful Norman magnate.'''[5]
2 CONT '''They had two children:'''[7]
2 CONT *Charles de Lorraine, Duc d'Elbeuf (1556–1605)[8]
2 CONT *Marie de Lorraine (21 August 1555 – c. 1605), styled Mademoiselle d'Elbeuf, married at Joinville on 10 November 1576 Charles de Lorraine-Guise, Duc d'Aumale and had issue.[9]
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT Death
2 CONT Recently installed in Provence in his capacity as commander of the Mediterranean fleet, he died in 1566, a heavy blow for the Guise family. In the wake of his death the young Duke of Guise and Charles, Duke of Mayenne decided to d
2 CONC epart the country, going on Crusade in Hungary.[36]
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ren%C3%A9_II_de_Lorraine,_Marquis_d%27Elbeuf
2 CONT _____
