1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fran%C3%A7ois_de_Bourbon,_Duke_of_Montpensier
2 CONT
2 CONT François de Bourbon (1542 – 4 June 1592) was the Duke of Montpensier and member of the House of Bourbon. He was the brother of Charlotte de Bourbon, Princess of Orange and wife of William the Silent, Prince of Orange. He was the g
2 CONC reat grand father of La Grande Mademoiselle cousin of Louis XIV.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT François was born in 1542 to Louis de Bourbon, Duke of Montpensier and his wife Jacqueline de Longvy. From birth he was known as the Dauphin of Auvergne until his father's death in 1582 when he inherited his father's titles and es
2 CONC tates. From then on he was styled the Duke of Montpensier; he also inherited the title Prince of Dombes as well as the Lordship of Châtellerault and Viscounty of Brosse.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a teenager, he actively took part in the war against the Huguenots. He also organised the prize of Saint-Jean-d'Angély in 1569 and fought against Protestants at Saintonge. In 1574, he was named Governor of Languedoc and the Dau
2 CONC phiné by Henry III of France. A zealous Roman Catholic, he stayed close to Henry III and didn't join the Holy League. At the death of Henry III, François allied himself with Henry IV of France, his own cousin, who took the French 
2 CONC throne in 1589.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died some time after he was created Governor of Normandy. He was succeeded by his son Henri de Bourbon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family life
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1566 he married Renée d'Anjou, only surviving daughter of Nicolas d'Anjou and Gabrielle de Mareuil. Renée was a great great great granddaughter of Louis II of Naples. François and Renée had one son:
2 CONT
2 CONT Henri de Bourbon, Duke of Montpensier (12 May 1573 – 27 February 1608) married Henriette Catherine de Joyeuse and had issue: 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Marie de Bourbon, Duchess of Montpensier (15 October 1605 – 4 June 1627) married Gaston d'Orléans and had issue: 
2 CONT
2 CONT      Anne Marie Louise d'Orléans, Duchess of Montpensier, La Grande Mademoiselle (29 May 1627 – 3 April 1693) died unmarried.
