1 DEAT
2 DATE 5 JAN 1633
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00024724&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Claude-François was born on 17 February 1590, the son of Evandelin Simon de Cusance, comte de Champlitte, baron de Belvoir, and Béatrice de Vergy. He was baron de Belvoir et de Saint-Julien, seigneur de Cusance, member o
2 CONC f the War Council, and colonel of a regiment of 3000 Burgundians in the service of Spain in Flanders. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 20 October 1612 he married Ernestine van Witthem, comtesse de Walhain, daughter of Jean van Witthem, vicomte de Sebourg, and Maria Margareta de Merode, marquise de Bergen-op-Zoom. They had four daughters of whom three, Béatrice
2 CONC , Madeleine and Marie Henriette, would have progeny, and two sons Clériadus, neither of whom had progeny. With the death of the younger Clériadus the house of Cusance died out, and the lordships of Belvoir, Cusance and Saint-Julie
2 CONC n reverted to Claude-François' eldest daughter Béatrice, who transferred them to her daughter from her second marriage, Anne de Lorraine, princesse de Lillebonne. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Claude-François' second daughter Madeleine married Graaf Albert van den Bergh, and his third, Marie Henriette, married first Ferdinand François de Rye de La Palud, marquis de Varambon, with whom she did not have progeny, then Char
2 CONC les Eugène, 2nd duc d'Arenberg. Claude-François died before 5 January in 1633.
