1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles,_Duke_of_Aumale
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles of Guise, duc d'Aumale (25 January 1555 – 1631, Brussels) was the son of Claude, Duke of Aumale and Louise de Brézé.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT One of the leaders of the Catholic League, he was at times governor of Picardy and Grand Veneur of France. He led a rebellion in Picardy in 1587, a prelude to open war between the House of Guise and Henry III of France. He was def
2 CONC eated at the Battle of Senlis on 17 May 1589 by the allied forces of Henry III and Henry of Navarre. Captured by Henry of Navarre at the Battle of Ivry, he died in exile.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Marie of Lorraine, daughter of René, Marquis of Elbeuf and Louise de Rieux. The princess was known as Mademoiselle d'Elbeuf, derived from her fathers title. The couple married at the Château de Joinville on 10 November 
2 CONC 1576, by whom he had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT  Charles (b. December 1580), d. young
2 CONT
2 CONT  Henri, d. young
2 CONT
2 CONT  Marguerite, d. young
2 CONT
2 CONT  Anne (1600 – 10 February 1638), Duchess of Aumale, married on 18 April 1618 Henri de Savoie, 4th Duc de Nemours
2 CONT
2 CONT  Marie, married Ambrosio, Marquis of Spinola in 1615
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles,_Duke_of_Aumale
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles, Duke of Aumale
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT 	This article does not cite any references or sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT Please help improve this article by adding citations to reliable sources. Unsourced material may be challenged and removed. (March 2010)
2 CONT
2 CONT Coat of Arms of the Dukes of Aumale
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles of Guise, duc d'Aumale (25 January 1555 – 1631, Brussels) was the son of Claude, Duke of Aumale and Louise de Brézé.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT One of the leaders of the Catholic League, he was at times governor of Picardy and Grand Veneur of France. He led a rebellion in Picardy in 1587, a prelude to open war between the House of Guise and Henry III of France. He was def
2 CONC eated at the Battle of Senlis on 17 May 1589 by the allied forces of Henry III and Henry of Navarre. Captured by Henry of Navarre at the Battle of Ivry, he died in exile.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Family
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Marie, daughter of René, Marquis of Elbeuf at the Château de Joinville on 10 November 1576, by whom he had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Charles (b. December 1580), d. young
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Henri, d. young
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Marguerite, d. young
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Anne (1600 – 10 February 1638), Duchess of Aumale, married on 18 April 1618 Henri de Savoie, 4th Duc de Nemours
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Marie, married Ambrosio, Marquis of Spinola in 1615
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceded by
2 CONT
2 CONT Claude 	Duke of Aumale
2 CONT
2 CONT 1573–1631 	Succeeded by
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne
2 CONT
2 CONT with Henri
2 CONT
