1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matthias,_Holy_Roman_Emperor
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthias (24 February 1557 – 20 March 1619) was Holy Roman Emperor from 1612, King of Hungary and Croatia from 1608 (as Matthias II) and King of Bohemia from 1611. He was a member of the House of Habsburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthias was born in the Austrian capital of Vienna to Maximilian II, Holy Roman Emperor and Maria of Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthias married Archduchess Anna of Austria, daughter of his uncle Archduke Ferdinand II of Austria, whose successor in Further Austria Matthias became in 1595. Their marriage did not produce surviving children.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1593 he was appointed governor of Austria by his brother, Emperor Rudolf II. He formed a close association there with the Bishop of Vienna, Melchior Klesl, who later became his chief adviser. In 1605 Matthias forced the ailing 
2 CONC emperor to allow him to deal with the Hungarian Protestant rebels. The result was the Peace of Vienna of 1606, which guaranteed religious freedom in Hungary. In the same year Matthias was recognized as head of the House of Habsbur
2 CONC g and as the future Holy Roman Emperor, as a result of Rudolf's illness. Allying himself with the estates of Hungary, Austria, and Moravia, Matthias forced his brother to yield rule of these lands to him in 1608; Rudolf later cede
2 CONC d Bohemia in 1611.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Matthias's accession as Holy Roman Emperor, his policy was dominated by Klesl, who hoped to bring about a compromise between Catholic and Protestant states within the Holy Roman Empire in order to strengthen it. Matthias had
2 CONC  already been forced to grant religious concessions to Protestants in Austria and Moravia, as well as in Hungary, when he had allied with them against Rudolf.
2 CONT
2 CONT His conciliatory policies were opposed by the more intransigent Catholic Habsburgs, particularly Matthias's brother Archduke Maximilian, who hoped to secure the succession for the inflexible Catholic Archduke Ferdinand (later Empe
2 CONC ror Ferdinand II). The start of the Bohemian Protestant revolt in 1618 provoked Maximilian to imprison Klesl and revise his policies. Matthias, old and ailing, was unable to prevent a takeover by Maximilian's faction. Ferdinand, w
2 CONC ho had already been crowned King of Bohemia (1617) and of Hungary (1618), succeeded Matthias as Holy Roman Emperor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthias died in Vienna in 1619.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT -------------------- -In 1591, he was knighted with a coat-of-arms to the House of Knights ("Housius Riders", Mounted Horsemen) by his second cousin, Emperor Ferdinand III, of Austria.
2 CONT
2 CONT -In 1612, succeeded his brother, Rudolph, and was crowned King of Hungary and Bohemia, 1619.
2 CONT
2 CONT -He died without issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT -He requested Ferdinand III to succeed him.
