2 CONT For other people named Anna of Austria, see Anna of Austria (disambiguation).
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna of Austria (Cigales, Valladolid, 1 November 1549 – Badajoz, 26 October 1580), was Queen consort of Spain and Portugal.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the first daughter of Maximilian II, Holy Roman Emperor and Maria of Spain. She was born in Spain, but lived in Vienna from the age of four.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents
2 CONT
