1 NAME Henri "Cadet la Perle" de Lorraine, Count of Harcourt
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 20 MAR 1601
1 DEAT
2 DATE 25 JUL 1666
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henri_de_Lorraine,_count_of_Harcourt '''Henri de Lorraine''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Henri de Lorraine (20 March 1601 - 25 July 1666, Royaumont Abbey), known as Cadet la Perle, was a French nobleman. He was count of Harcourt, count of Armagnac, count of Brionne and viscount of Marsan. He was the younger son of Cha
2 CONC rles I, Duke of Elbeuf and his wife Marguerite de Chabot, countess of Charny.
2 CONT
2 CONT He did his first military service at the siege of Prague in November 1620 and because of his bravoury he was nicknamed Cadet la Perle by his companions after the pearl he wore in his ear.
2 CONT
2 CONT In France he fought the Protestants and took part in the Siege of La Rochelle (1627–1628) and Saint-Jean-d'Angély. He was made a knight in the Order of the Holy Spirit in 1633, Grand Squire of France in 1643 and Seneschal of Burgu
2 CONC ndy.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1637 he fought in Piedmont during the Franco-Spanish War (1635-1659), where he defeated a Spanish army, very superieur in numbers near Chieri. He was also in charge of the Siege of Turin (1640), where he took the city after a s
2 CONC iege of three months. He then fought in Sardinia and Catalonia, where he was named viceroy in 1645.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the Fronde, he remained loyal to the regent-queen Anne of Austria, but clashed with Mazarin, and retreated in the Alsace.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Marriage and issue He married in February 1639 with Marguerite-Philippe du Cambout (1622–1674), and had 6 children :
2 CONT
2 CONT Armande Henriette (1640–1684), abbess of Soissons;
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis, Count of Armagnac (1641–1718), of Charny and of Brionne and ancestor of prince Albert II of Monaco through his daughter Marie of Lorraine, who was forced by King Louis XIV to marry Antonio I of Monaco ; a great grand daught
2 CONC er, Princess Joséphine of Lorraine, was the grand mother of Charles Albert of Sardinia, the present House of Savoy descend from this line;
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippe (1643–1702), called chevalier de Lorraine and lover of Philippe I, Duke of Orléans
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfonse Louis (1644–1689), abbot of Royaumont, called chevalier d'Harcourt ;
2 CONT
2 CONT Raimond Bérenger (1647–1686), abbot of Faron de Meaux ; Charles (1648–1708), Viscount then Count of Marsan had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henri_de_Lorraine-Harcourt
