1 NOTE {geni:about_me} REFN: 463 "The Compendium of American Genealogy" page 220-221: Jean Victor Jules (Fennell) (b 1650), Count de Valois, Baron of Bele Fonta; follower of Peter Waldo, religious reformer; fled from Lyons, France to Eng
2 CONC land, 1685, thence to New York were he became a successful business man. Married Elizabeth Hartwell Antoine Charles Louis de Valois was the illegitimate son of Louis Emmanuel de Valois.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was legitimized in 1677 and made Chevalier d'Angouleme; Mestre de camp du régiment de La Rouche-sur-Yon; Chevalier de l'ordre de Saint-Lazare.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fathered an illegitimate daughter.  Some Americans believe that his daughter was Clothilde de Valois Zeller.  No documentation has been found which would confirm that a person with that name ever existed.* Reference: [https://w
2 CONC ww.findagrave.com/memorial/170891805/antoine-charles_louis-de_valois Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 11 2020, 15:36:49 UTC''
