2 CONT
2 CONT Louis de Bourbon, Prince of Condé (8 September 1621 – 11 December 1686) was a French general and the most famous representative of the Condé branch of the House of Bourbon. Prior to his father's death in 1646, he was styled the Du
2 CONC c d'Enghien. For his military prowess he was renowned as le Grand Condé.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis II de Bourbon-Condé, Prince de Condé
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #403600, b. 1621, d. 1686
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=1 Nov 2009
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis II de Bourbon-Condé, Prince de Condé was born in 1621. He was the son of Henri II de Bourbon-Condé, Prince de Condé and Charlotte de Montmorency. He married Claire-Clemence de Maille-Breze in 1643 at Paris, France. (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1686
2 CONT
