1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===LADY MARY STEWART===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Mary Stewart, is the only daughter of James, Earl of Moray, and his Countess, Lady Anne Gordon. [https://archive.org/details/chiefsofgrantmv100fras/page/249/mode/1up The Chiefs of Grant I: 249]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/chiefsofgrantmv100fras/page/n6/mode/1up The Chiefs of Grant. By William Fraser, LL.D. Vol. I. Memoirs (Edinburgh, 1883), 545 pp.]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/chiefsofgrantv200fras/page/n4/mode/1up The Chiefs of Grant. By William Fraser, LL.D. Vol. II. Correspondence (Edinburgh, 1883), 568 pp.]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/chiefsofgrantmv300fras/page/n4/mode/1up The Chiefs of Grant. By William Fraser, LL.D. Vol. III. Charters (Edinburgh, 1883), 597 pp. including indexes]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Stewart
2 CONT Birth abt 1605 Death 18 Dec 1662 Age: 57 Father James Stewart 3rd Earl of Moray, M (1581-1638) Mother Anne Gordon, F (~1590-1674) Spouses: 1 James Grant 7th Earl of Freuchie, M Birth 24 Jun 1616, Freuchie, Perth, Scotland Death 10
2 CONC  Oct 1663, Edinburgh, Scotland Age: 47 Father Sir Knight John Grant 6th Earl of Freuchie, M (1596-1637) Mother Mary Ogilvie, F (~1600->1646) Marriage 24 Apr 1640 Children: Anna, F (~1645-) Ludovic, M (1652-1716) Patrick, M (-1693)
2 CONC  Mary, F Margaret, F Notes for James (Spouse 1) The oldest family portraits at Castle Grant are those of James Grant and his wife Mary Stewart. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 18 Dec 1662 Buried 	30 Dec 1662 	Duthil, Inverness-shire, Scotland Person ID 	I614004 	Stewart Genealogy Last Modified 	5 Jun 2013 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father 	Ancestors James Stewart, 3rd Earl of Moray,  b. Abt 1581,  d. 6 Aug 1638, Darnaway, Dyke and Moy, Moray, Scotland   (Age ~ 57 years)  Mother 	Ancestors Anne Gordon,  b. Abt 1591 Married 	Abt 2 Oct 1607  Family ID 	F306723 
2 CONC  	Group Sheet  |  Family Chart
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 	Ancestors James Grant, laird of Freuchie,   b. 24 Jun 1616 of, Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland    d. 1663, Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland   (Age 46 years)  Married 	24-25 Apr 1640  	Elgin, Moray, Scotland  Children  	
2 CONC  +	1. Ludovich Grant, laird of Freuchie,   b. of, Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland   d. Nov 1716, Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland 
2 CONT  	2. Lieutenant-Colonel Patrick Grant,   b. of, Wester Elchies  d. Jan 1692/93
2 CONT  	3. Anna Grant,   b. of, Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland 
2 CONT  	4. Mary Grant,   b. of, Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland 
2 CONT  	5. Margaret Grant,   b. of, Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland 
2 CONT  	6. [Unknown] Grant,   b. of, Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland  d. 1650 Family ID 	F318205  	Group Sheet  |  Family Chart
2 CONT
2 CONT 15th - 16th centuries
2 CONT
2 CONT The castle is a Z-plan tower house that dates from the fifteenth century. The lands had been held by the Clan Comyn but passed to the Grants in the fifteenth century and it became their main stronghold.
2 CONT
2 CONT The castle was originally named Freuchie Castle and James Grant of Freuchie supported James V of Scotland. 17th - 18th centuries
2 CONT
2 CONT Although the Grants were Protestants they joined James Graham, 1st Marquess of Montrose during the Scottish Civil War in the 1640s. The name of the castle changed from Freuchie Castle to Castle Grant in 1694 when the lands were ma
2 CONC de into the regality of Grant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ludovick Grant, the eighth laird supported the Hanoverians against the Stewarts and fought against the Jacobites in both the Jacobite rising of 1715 and the Jacobite rising of 1745.[1] However, Castle Grant was occupied by the Jac
2 CONC obites.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Stewart-3018
2 CONT
2 CONT https://thepeerage.com/p18875.htm#i188743
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/about/LBLL-4BY
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/152073726/mary-grant
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Mary Stuart was the daughter of James Stuart, 3rd Earl of Moray and Lady Anne Gordon. She married James Grant, 7th of Freuchie, son of Sir John Grant, 6th of Freuchie and Mary Ogilvy, on 24 April 1640. She died on 18 December
2 CONC  1662.
2 CONT
2 CONT From 24 April 1640, her married name became Grant. Her
2 CONT husband was buried on 10 October 1663.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lady Mary Stuart and James Grant, 7th of Freuchie
2 CONT 1. Anne Grant
2 CONT 2. Mary Grant
2 CONT 3. Margaret Grant
2 CONT 4. Ludovic Grant, 8th of Freuchie and 1st of Grant, nicknamed "the Highland king" b. 1641, d. 1714.
2 CONT 5. Patrick Grant of Wester Elchies b. c 1645, d. Jan 1693.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Paul, James Balfour. "The Scots Peerage : founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility of that kingdom", Edinburgh: David Douglas, 1909, Vol. 
2 CONC VI, Archive.,org, p. 320 < [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06paul/page/320/mode/2up Archive.Org] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The Earl married, by arrangement of the King in an endeavour to heal the feud between the two families, Anne Gordon, eldest daughter of George, first Marquess of Huntly; contract 2 October 1607.* By her he had issue : —
2 CONT * 1. James, fourth Earl of Moray.
2 CONT * 2. George, died at Edinburgh, unmarried.
2 CONT * 3. Margaret, married, about 25 April 1640, against the wishes of her family, to James Grant of French ie. She died 18 December 1662, and was buried 30, at Duthil.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
