1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir John Gordon, of Haddo</strong>, only son and heir of George Gordon, by Margaret, daughter of Sir Alexander Bannerman, of Elsick, which George (who died v.p. October 1610) was 1st son and heir apparent of James Gordon,
2 CONC  of Methlic and Haddo, was born early in 1610); succeeded his grandfather in November 1624; was next in command of the Royal forces to oppose the Covenanters, and was in the action of Turreff in 1639. He joined the King at Newark,
2 CONC  and was by him created a Baronet [S], 13 August 1642, with remainder to his heirs male of his body. In October 1643 he protested against the Covenant; was beseiged in his house at Kelly, and taken prisoner at its surrender, 8 May
2 CONC  1644; was found guilty of treason, and accordingly beheaded at Edinburgh, 19 July following, aged 34. He married in 1630, Mary, daughter of William Forbes of Tolquhoun. She survived him."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n469/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 451
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/155273591/john_(sir)-gordon
2 CONT
2 CONT John (Sir) Gordon
2 CONT BIRTH	1610 Aberdeen City, Scotland DEATH	19 Jun 1644 (aged 33–34) City of Edinburgh, Scotland BURIAL	 Saint Giles Cathedral Edinburgh, City of Edinburgh, Scotland  MEMORIAL ID	155273591 · View Source
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/155273591/john_(sir)-gordon
2 CONT
2 CONT John (Sir) Gordon BIRTH	1610 Aberdeen City, Scotland DEATH	19 Jun 1644 (aged 33–34) City of Edinburgh, Scotland BURIAL	 Saint Giles Cathedral Edinburgh, City of Edinburgh, Scotland  MEMORIAL ID	155273591 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members Parents Photo	 George Gordon 1583–1610
2 CONT
2 CONT Photo	 Margaret Bannerman Gordon 1589 – unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse Photo	 Mary Forbes Gordon 1614 – unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings Photo	 John Gordon 1610–1644
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription SIR JOHN GORDON Bart of Haddo Was imprisoned for conscience sake in a small church which then formed part of this Cathedral and became known as "Haddo's Hole". He was executed on Jun 19th 1644.  This tablet is erected 
2 CONC in his memory by his descendant JOHN CAMPBELL GORDON, Marquis of Aberdeen & Temair, KT 1933. Gravesite Details * Cenotaph
2 CONT
