1 OCCU Countess of Annandale
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The fact that there were two Henrietta Douglas women, close to the same age and born approximately the same time, has led to a lot of confusion. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anyone working on this line should be careful to get the right one!
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Lady Henrietta Douglas''' was born circa 1633.2 She was the daughter of William Douglas, 1st Marquess of Douglas and Lady Mary Gordon.1 A contract for the marriage of Lady Henrietta Douglas and James Johnstone, 1st Earl of Anna
2 CONC ndale and Hartfell was signed on 29 May 1645.1,2 She died on 1 June 1673.1
2 CONT
2 CONT From after 29 May 1645, her married name became Johnstone. After her marriage, Lady Henrietta Douglas was styled as Countess of Hartfell on 1 October 1653. After her marriage, Lady Henrietta Douglas was styled as Countess of Annan
2 CONC dale and Hartfell on 13 February 1660/61.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/annandaleh1662.htm#ANNANDALE_1662_1 CracroftsPeerage]:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Henrietta Douglas (b.c. 1633; d. 1 Jun 1673), 1st dau. of William [Douglas], 1st Marquess of Douglas, by his second wife Lady Mary Gordon, 3rd dau. of George [Gordon], 1st Marquess of Huntly.  Married 29 May 1645 to 
2 CONT
2 CONT James [Johnstone], 2nd Earl of Hartfell later 1st Earl of Annandale and Hartfell, PC 1st son and heir of James [Johnstone], 1st Earl of Hartfell, by his first wife Lady Margaret Douglas, 1st dau. of William [Douglas], 1st Earl of 
2 CONC Queensberry born 1625, died 17 Jul 1672.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 11 children (4 sons, 7 daughters) of James Johnstone, 1st Earl of Annandale and Hartfell and Lady Henrietta Douglas were:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Hon James Johnstone, styled Lord Johnstone (b. 17 Dec 1660; dvp. 1661/2)
2 CONT * 2. Hon William Johnstone, later 2nd Earl of Annandale and Hartfell later 1st Marquess of Annandale
2 CONT * 3. Maj-Gen Hon John Johnstone, a professional soldier, led the Jacobite mutiny of the Royal Scots Regiment 1689, Colonel in the Jacobite and French armies, commanded the Royal Saxon Army, commanded the Polish Cavalry Division (b
2 CONC . 3 Sep 1665; dspm. 29 Dec 1714), mar. 19 Jun 1713 Countess Catherine Christine von Ahlefeldt (mar. (2) 1722 Duke of Glucksburg; dsps. 1726), 1st dau. of Count Detler Sievert von Ahlefeldt, and had issue
2 CONT * 4. Hon George Johnstone (b. 21 Jun 1667; d. 10 May 1674)
2 CONT * 1. Lady Mary Johnstone (b. 31 Jan 1651/2; d. 8 Apr 1681), mar. 8 Mar 1670 as his first wife William [Lindsay], 18th Earl of Crawford, and had issue
2 CONT * 2. Lady Margaret Johnstone (b. 14 Aug 1654; d. 1726), mar. after 14 Sep 1678 Sir James Montgomerie of Skelmorlie (d. Sep 1694), and had issue
2 CONT * 3. Lady Henrietta Johnstone (b. 18 Jan 1657; dvp. young)
2 CONT * 4. Lady Janet Johnstone (b. 18 Jun 1858; dvp. young)
2 CONT * 5. Lady Isabel Johnstone (b. 28 Apr 1659; dvp. young)
2 CONT * 6. Lady Henrietta Johnstone (b. 21 Jan 1668/9), mar. 15 May 1684 Sir John Carmichael of Bonningtoun, and had issue
2 CONT * 7. Lady Anna Johnstone (b. 30 Jul 1671; d. Jun 1675)
