1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == DAVID ERSKINE, LORD CARDROSS ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''David Erskine, here treated: "who on the death of his grandfather John, Earl of Mar, on 14 December 1634, succeeded to the lordship of Cardross. He was one of the few peers who opposed the surrender of King Oharles I. to the Cr
2 CONC omwellians at Newcastle in 1646. On 18 February 1664 he had a charter of the lordship of Cardross, with power of nominating his successor in the Peerage, which failing, with remainder to the heirs-male of his body, whom failing to
2 CONC  his heirs and assigns whomsoever. He died in 1671. He married, first, contract dated 9 August 1645, Anne, fifth daughter of Sir Thomas Hope of Craighall, Bart., Lord Advocate. He married, secondly, in 1655, Mary, youngest daughte
2 CONC r of Sir George Bruce of Carnock, and sister of Edward, Earl of Kincardine."  [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/page/365/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: 365-6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 December 1636: Bond by Dame Marie Stewart, wife of the deceased John, [2nd] Earl of Mar, to Dame Margaret Ballenden, mother of David, Lord Cardross, for £500 Scots as compensation for the lands of Littill Coldoch alias Spitt
2 CONC eltoun and Arnebeg which the said deceased Earl had granted to deceased Henry Erskine, Lord Cardross, his son, whom failing his other sons, in Bond, dated 31 July 1623. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/detai
2 CONC ls.aspx?reference=GD15%2f152&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=David+lord+cardross&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1630&dt=1675&di=n National Records of Scotland, Erskine family of Cardross, Perthshire, reference GD15/152]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''c. 1640: Disposition by Adam Cunynghame of Boquhane, with consent of Elizabeth Houstoune, his spouse, to David, Lord Cardross, and Dame Margaret Bellenden, Lady Cardross, his tutrix dative, of lands of Eister Garden. [https://c
