2 CONT * Author's Subject: Re: Habsburg Bastards 
2 CONT * Date Written: Thu, 29 Jun 1995 11:06:41 EST 
2 CONT * Date Posted: Fri, 29 Jun 1995 12:06:41 -0400
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is a postscript to the earlier discussion of Habsburg bastards.  N.B. that the remains no evidence of ANY after 1618 or before 1800.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Emperor Rudolf II (1552-1612), who never married, had 6 illegitimate children, all titled Markgraf or Markgraefin of Austria: Dorothea (a nun), Elizabeth (a nun), Karl (a soldier), Julius (born about 1586) Herr von Krummau who be
2 CONC came insane and died 1609 at Krummau.  The last two were by Euphemia von Rosenthal: '''Matthias''' who, in 1608, hoped to become a Cardinal; he didn't, joined the army and in 1618 married a "Sicilian princess", died in Germany in 
2 CONC 1626.  '''Charlotte''' died in Mechelen (now in Belgium) in 1662; in 1608 she married Francois Thomas d'Oizelet, Comte de Cantecroy.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.maltagenealogy.com/aragona
2 CONT
2 CONT 13.1.1.3.3.3.2.1.1.1.1.5.4. Joanna Galea married 1609 Valletta to '''Don Giovanni Mattias di Österreich''', (created Knight of the Holy Roman Empire) (d. 1626 Wien), [genealogy], (illegitimate son of RUDOLF II, Holy Roman Emperor 
2 CONC and Euphemia von Rosenthal), with issue .
2 CONT
2 CONT 13.1.1.3.3.3.2.1.1.1.1.5.4.1. Donna Imperia di Österreich, 1624: Baroness von Rosenthal, married 1617 Palermo, Sicily to Vincenzo de Licata, married (2) 1625 Birkirkara to Salvatore Micallef, with issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT E5. [by Euphemia von Rosenthal] '''Matthias''', +Wien IX.1626; m.NN, a Sicilian lady
