2 CONT Anna Gonzaga (Anna Marie; 1616 – 6 July 1684) 
2 CONT was an Italian French noblewoman and salonist. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The youngest daughter of Charles Gonzaga, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke of Mantua and Montferrat, and Catherine de Mayenne 
2 CONT (herself daughter of Charles, Duke of Mayenne), Anna was "
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Palatine" as the wife of Edward of the Palatinate, her husband and 
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandson of King James I of England and uncle to King George I of Great Britain. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She bore Edward three children, all daughters. Had Anna not converted Edward to Catholicism, the English throne might have passed to their descendants
2 CONT
