1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ben notes: Information about Paul's existence is better documented elsewhere. The information that I have here is from another family tree, where the compiler was apparently a big fan of the Broderbund World Family
2 CONC  Tree genealogical date estimation system (I'm not, at least as far as documenting family trees go):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/h/e/n/Joseph--Henninger-Tello/GENE2-0003.html
2 CONT
2 CONT PAUL [3] MARLET (JOSUE (JOSIAS) [2] MERLE, UNKNOWN [1]) was born Abt. 1630 in Roucy, Champagne, FRANCE, and died WFT Est. 1667-1721 in Mannheim, GERMANY. He married ELIZABETH MOREAU WFT Est. 1645-1679. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of PAUL MARLET and ELIZABETH MOREAU are: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. GEDEON [4] MERLET, b. September 18, 1657; d. WFT Est. 1658-1747. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. HENRY MERLET, b. February 21, 1659; d. WFT Est. 1660-1749. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. NOE MERLET, b. May 07, 1662; d. WFT Est. 1663-1756. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. JEANNE MERLET, b. August 31, 1664; d. WFT Est. 1665-1758. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I'm going to wait for the better source material before entering the rest of the names onto the tree.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Born in Roucy in the Champagne Province of France, Fled religious persecution in France.  Moved to Leiden in the province of Zuid Holland in the Netherlands, prior to settling in Mannheim in the Palatinate of Germany (now the stat
2 CONC e of Baden-Wuerttemburg, Germany).  Married 20 Feb1655 in the French Reformed Church at Mannheim, Germany to Elizabeth Moreau.
