1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guy_Aldonce_de_Durfort_de_Lorges
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy Aldonce de Durfort, duc de Lorges, marshal of France, (22 August 1630 – 22 October 1702), was a French nobleman and soldier.
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy Aldonce was the fourth son of Guy Aldonce de Durfort (1605-1665), marquis of Duras, count of Rozan and of Lorges, maréchal de camp, and Élisabeth de La Tour d'Auvergne, daughter of Henri de La Tour d'Auvergne and the sister of
2 CONC  Turenne.
2 CONT
2 CONT His brother, Jacques Henri de Durfort de Duras, was also a Marshal of France. It is possible that the fame of their uncle played a major part in the military career of Jacques-Henri and Guy Aldonce.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the War of the Grand Alliance he commanded the French army in Germany from 1690 to 1695. On 27 September 1692, he defeated 4,000 imperial cavalry under the command of Frederick Charles, Duke of Württemberg-Winnental; the follow
2 CONC ing year in 1693, and took the city of Heidelberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Gabrielle de Frémont, daughter of the keeper of the kIng's jewels. Many of his friends considered that he had married socially beneath him, but the marriage was a happy one, and even his son-in-law Saint-Simon, who disa
2 CONC pproved of marriage between the classes, admitted that she was an admirable wife. They has one son and five daughters. Marie Gabrielle de Durfort de Lorges, his eldest daughter married Louis de Rouvroy, duc de Saint-Simon. Another
2 CONC  daughter, Geneviève, married Antoine Nompar de Caumont, duke of Lauzun. Saint-Simon praises his father-in-law warmly in his memoirs, describing him as highly principled, frank, upright, good-natured, sincere and the most truthful
2 CONC  man alive. He supplied his son-in-law with useful material for his memoirs, particularly on the early relations between Louis XIV and Madame de Maintenon.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Saint-Simon, his death was caused by an operation to remove a kidney-stone: the inexperienced surgeon mishandled the operation and Guy Aldonce died in agony, which he endured with great courage.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT lire http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guy_Aldonce_II_de_Durfort
