2 CONT      Louise Diane d'Orléans was born on 27 June 1716 at Paris, France. (2) 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Philippe II d'Orléans, Duc d'Orléans and Françoise Marie de Bourbon. (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Louis François I de Bourbon, Prince de Conti, son of Louis Armand II de Bourbon, Prince de Conti and Louise Elizabeth de Condé, on 22 January 1732 at Versailles, Île-de-France, France. (2) 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 26 September 1736 at age 20 at Château d'Issy, Paris, France. (2) She was buried at Church of St. André des Arts, Paris, France. (2)
2 CONT
2 CONT      Louise Diane d'Orléans was also known as Mademoiselle de Chartres as of after 1717. (2)
