2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p2508.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Stuart, 5th Earl of Moray''' 
2 CONT * Baptised on 8 May 1634.
2 CONT * Son of James Stuart, 4th Earl of Moray and Lady Margaret Home.
2 CONT * Married '''Emilia Balfour''', daughter of Sir William Balfour of Pitcullo, circa 1658.
2 CONT * Died on 1 November 1700 at age 66.
2 CONT * Succeeded to the title of 
2 CONT >* 5th Lord Doune [S., 1581] on 4 March 1653.1
2 CONT >* 3rd Lord Saint Colme [S., 1620] on 4 March 1653.
2 CONT * Gained the title of 5th Earl of Moray [S., 1562] on 4 March 1653.
2 CONT * Succeeded to the title of 
2 CONT >* 5th Lord Abernethy [S., 1562] on 4 March 1653.
2 CONT >* 5th Lord Strathdearn [S., 1563] on 4 March 1653.
2 CONT * In 1654 he was fined £3,500 as a Royalist.
2 CONT * Invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) in February 1660/61.
2 CONT * Held the office of 
2 CONT >* Lord Justice General [Scotland] in 1675/76.
2 CONT >* Lord of Treasury in 1678
2 CONT >*  Secretary of State in 1680
2 CONT >* Extraordinary Lord of Session in 1680
2 CONT >* Lord High Commissioner [Scotland] in 1686
2 CONT * In 1678 he raised a regiment of Highlanders.
2 CONT * Invested as a Knight, Order of the Thistle (K.T.) in 1687.
2 CONT * In 1688 he was deprived of his offices.
2 CONT * In 1690 he was imprisoned as a suspected Jacobite. '''Children of Alexander Stuart, 5th Earl of Moray and Emilia Balfour'''
2 CONT * James Stuart, Lord Doune b. b 1660, d. 1685
2 CONT * Charles Stuart, 6th Earl of Moray b. c 1660, d. 7 Oct 1735
2 CONT * Hon. John Stuart b. a 1661, d. b 1700
2 CONT * Francis Stuart, 7th Earl of Moray b. 4 Sep 1673, d. 11 Dec 1739<br/>
2 CONT <span>
2 CONT ----
