1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Image 
2 CONT at http://www.bbc.co.uk/arts/yourpaintings/paintings/george-1st-earl-of-aberdeen-196796
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT George Gordon of Haddo, 1st Earl of Aberdeen was born on 3 October 1637. He was the son of Sir John Gordon, 1st Bt. and Mary Forbes. A contract for the marriage of George Gordon of Haddo, 1st Earl of Aberdeen and Anne Lockhart was
2 CONC  signed in 1671. He died on 20 April 1720 at age 82 at Kellie, Scotland. He succeeded to the title of 3rd Baronet Gordon, of Haddo, co. Aberdeen [S., 1642] in 1665. He was admitted to an Advocate on 7 February 1668.He held the off
2 CONC ice of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Aberdeen between 1669 and 1674. He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Aberdeen in 1678. He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) in 1678. He held the office of Senator of 
2 CONC the College of Justice in 1680. He held the office of a Lord of Session between 1 June 1680 and June 1684. He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Aberdeen between 1681 and 1682. He held the office of President of th
2 CONC e Session between  November 1681 and June 1684. He held the office of High Chancellor [Scotland] between 1 May 1682 and June 1684. He was created 1st Viscount of Formartine [Scotland] on 30 November 1682. He was created 1st Lord H
2 CONC addo, Methlick, Tarves and Kellie [Scotland] on 30 November 1682.He was created 1st Earl of Aberdeen [Scotland] on 30 November 1682. His last will was dated 15 May 1706. In 1708 at Edinburgh Castle, Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland
2 CONC , he was held prisoner.
2 CONT
