2 DATE 1 JUL 1708
2 ADDR
3 CITY Inch
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR JAMES MURRAY OF PHILIPHAUGH Lord Philiphaugh===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Member of the Convention of Estates (1678); Member of the Scottish Parliament (1678); Sheriff or Forres and Urquart of Meldrum (1680); Senator of the College of Justice (1685);  Sheriff principal of Selkirk (1689)' 
2 CONC Lord Clerk Registrar (1702)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir James Murray of Philiphaugh married Anna Hepburn. [http://www.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/70/mode/2up Murray Heraldry: 284] The marriage was booked on 24 April 1675, at Edinburgh in Midlothian, Scotland. 
2 CONC {national Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Marriages, reference OPR.685/1/44]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir James Murray of Philiphaugh married Margaret Don. [http://www.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/70/mode/2up Murray Heraldry: 284]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children of Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 September 1689: Warrant for Commission under Great Seal in favour of James Murray of Philiphaugh as sheriff-principal of Selkirk. Signed by William III. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?ref
2 CONC erence=GD26%2f11%2f34&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+murray+of+Philiphaugh&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Leslie family, Earls of Leven and Melville, reference GD26/11/34]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 December 1702: Minutes of a Privy Council held 1 December 1702 - Sederunt 8 Earls, 8 Lords, Lord Provost of Edinburgh and Mr Francis Montgomery, at which meeting of Privy Council were presented three Commissions under the gre
2 CONC at Seal: 1st James Earl of Seafield to be Lord High Chancellor of Scotland; 2nd George Viscount of Tarbat to be Conjunct Secretary of State for Scotland; 3rd Sir James Murray of Philiphaugh to be Lord Clerk Register etc. [http://c
2 CONC atalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD305%2f1%2f161%2f67&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+murray+of+Philiphaugh&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the MacKenzie Famil
2 CONC y, Earls of Cromartie, reference GD305/1/161/67]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 June 1703: Ratification by Sir James Murray of Philiphaugh, Clerk Register, of commission to Mr William Foulis as clerk and keeper of GRS and of PRS Edinburgh and appointment of said Mr William to mark the volumes. [http://c
2 CONC atalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=SRO1%2f46&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+murray+of+Philiphaugh&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Records originally at Edinburgh Castle a
2 CONC nd Laigh Parliament House, reference SRO1/46]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biographical Summaries===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Murray of Philiphaugh. Eldest son of Sir John Murray of Philiphaugh, by Ann, daughter of Sir Archibald Douglas of Cavers was born in 1655. He sat in the convention of estates which assembled . . . . . being appointed an o
2 CONC rdinary Lord on the 28th October, he took his seat as <strong>Lord Philiphaugh</strong> on the 1st November 1689 . . . . . n the following year Lord Philiphaugh produced a commission en the first June nominating him a second time 
2 CONC Lord Register which appointment he retained as also his office of judge till his death which took place at Inch on Sunday 1st July 1708."'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/anhistoricalacc00haiggoog/page/n467/mode/1up An Historical Account of the Senators of the College of Justice: From Its Institution in MDXXXII. By George Brunton (David Haig; 1832;), pp.434-36]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''284) Sir James Murray of Philiphaugh, born 1655 ; died 1st July 1708. He was served heir to his father 8th November 1677; and was appointed a Senator of the College of Justice, as Lord Philiphaugh, 1689. He was M.P. for Selkirk
2 CONC shire 1678-1702, and was appointed Lord Clerk Register 1705. He married, first, at Edinburgh, 24th April 1678, Anne, daughter of Hepburn of Blackcastle, who died s.p. He married, second, Margaret, daughter of Sir Alexander Don of 
2 CONC Newton, and had issue: -'''
2 CONT
2 CONT #  '''John (No. 285 below)'''
2 CONT #  '''James Murray, died unmarried'''
2 CONT #  '''Alexander Murray, died unmarried'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/70/mode/2up The heraldry of the Murrays: with notes on all the males of the family, descriptions of the arms, plates and pedigrees. By G. Harvey Johnston (1910) p. 70, par
2 CONC a. 284]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT == SIR JAMES MURRAY OF PHILIPHAUGH ==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Senator of the College of Justice, where he sat as Lord Philiphaugh; Scottish judge and Politician, who twice served as Lord Clerk Register, from November 1702 to June 1704 and from April 1705 to July 1708===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Murray,_Lord_Philiphaugh Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
