2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 November 1686: Propositions for a Contract of Marriage between the Earl of Panmure and Lady Margaret Hamilton, daughter of the Duke of Hamilton. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=
2 CONC GD103%2f2%2f4%2f33&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+hamilton&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of Society of Antiquaries of Scotland, reference GD103/2/4/33]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 February 1687: Marriage contract between James, Earl of Panmure, and Lady Margaret Hamilton, youngest daughter of William, Duke of Hamilton, with consent of her father and mother. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlin
2 CONC ecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD45%2f17%2f641&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+hamilton&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ramsay Family, Earls of Dalhousie, reference GD45/17/641]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 January 1708: Draft disposition by James, Earl of Panmure, to James Maule, eldest son of Mr. Harry Maule of Kelly, brother of the said Earl, of the title of Earl of Panmure and all his lands and other heritages reserving to 
2 CONC himself the life-rent thereof and to Margaret, Countess of Panmure, certain liferents, under condition of redemption to a son or daughter of the said Earl, should he have any. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue
2 CONC /details.aspx?reference=GD45%2f16%2f34&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+maule&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1730&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Maule Family, Earls of Dalhousie, reference GD45/16/34]'''
