1 NOTE James, born 1662, served as Lord High Treasurer of Scotland as well as Secretary of State and Lord High Commissioner, but he is best known as the minister who, in 1707, drafted the "Act of Union" between England and Scotland. As a
2 CONC  result, he
2 CONT joined the ranks of only two other Scots and was conferred the honor of a Dukedom in England. James died in 1711, but prior to his death the 2nd Duke arranged for the Marquissate and Earldom of Queensberry to pass to his eldest so
2 CONC n, James, who
2 CONT was widely known to be insane. The greater responsibility of the Dukedom, because of James' diminished mental state, was passed to the Duke's 2nd son, Charles.
