1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Golden Fleece - Knights: Spanish Branch===
2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antoine_Charles_IV_de_Gramont '''Antoine IV, duc de Gramont ''']
2 CONT * From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Antoine Charles IV de Gramont, comte de Guiche, 3rd Duke de Gramont, comte de Louvigny, Souverain de Bidache (1641 – October 25, 1720) was a French diplomat.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Antoine III de Gramont and Françoise-Marguerite du Plessis de Chivré, Richelieu's niece.
2 CONT
2 CONT He distinguished himself in the King’s armies during the campaign against Holland in 1672 and during the Siege of Besançon (1674) in the Franco-Dutch War. Later he was Ambassador extraordinary in Spain, Viceroy of Navarre and Béar
2 CONC n, and governor of Bayonne. He was a Knight of the King's order and '''Knight of the Golden Fleece'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT * He married in 1668 Marie Charlotte de Castelnau (1648 – January 29, 1694), daughter of Marshal Castelnau.
2 CONT * They had two children :
2 CONT # Antoine V de Gramont (1672–1725), 4th Duke of Gramont.
2 CONT # Catherine-Charlotte (died 1739), married Louis François, duc de Boufflers
2 CONT * After his wife death he married in 1710 Anne Baillet de La Cour.
