1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Vincenzo De Licata married 1624 in Palermo, Sicilia, Italy Donna Imperia di Osterreich, Cr 1624: Baroness von Rosenthal in Germany,   Her descendants are Hereditary Knights of the Holy Roman Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://gw.geneanet.org/sasciak?lang=en&iz=40&p=joanna&n=galea
2 CONT
2 CONT *Joanna Galea maried in 1609 Valletta, Malta, to [https://www.geni.com/people/Mattias-Giovanni-d-Austria/6000000015264962206 Mattias Giovanni di Österreich] (Parents : M Rudolph III Holy Roman Emperor Habsburg 1552-1612 &  F Euphe
2 CONC mia von Rosenthal) with 
2 CONT **F '''Imperia Agata di Österreich'''  Married in 1624, Palermo, Sicily, Italy, to Vincenzo de Licata with
2 CONT *** M Andrea de Licata Married 8 September 1649, Attard, Malta, to Valenza Mizzi
2 CONT *** M Antonio Delicata Married 13 June 1647, Siggiewi, Malta, to Vincenza Azzopardi with :
2 CONT **** M Pietro Licata
2 CONT *** F Caterina de Licata Married in 1628, Zebbug, Malta, to Gio Maria Buttigieg
2 CONT *** F Antonia de Licata
2 CONT *** F Geronima de Licata
2 CONT *** F Angelica de Licata
2 CONT *** M Blasco de Licata
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.maltagenealogy.com/aragona
2 CONT
2 CONT 13.1.1.3.3.3.2.1.1.1.1.5.4. Joanna Galea married 1609 Valletta to [https://www.geni.com/people/Mattias-Giovanni-d-Austria/6000000015264962206 Don Giovanni Mattias di Österreich], (created Knight of the Holy Roman Empire) (d. 1626 
2 CONC Wien), [genealogy], (illegitimate son of RUDOLF II, Holy Roman Emperor and Euphemia von Rosenthal), with issue .
2 CONT
2 CONT 13.1.1.3.3.3.2.1.1.1.1.5.4.1. Donna''' Imperia di Österreich''', 1624: Baroness von Rosenthal, married 1617 Palermo, Sicily to Vincenzo de Licata, married (2) 1625 Birkirkara to Salvatore Micallef, with issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.maltagenealogy.com/maltesenobles75 
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference is often found in Malta, to the title “Knight of the Holy Roman Empire”. The Holy Roman Empire was dissolved in 1806.
2 CONT
2 CONT This is a title of Nobility which predates all of the titles created by the Grandmasters of the Order of Saint John during their rule over the Maltese Islands. The title was conferred “motu proprio” by the Holy Roman Emperors in f
2 CONC avour of Giacomo Testaferrata in 1637, and Massimiliano Balzano in 1698. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The first title granted by the Grand Masters was that of Barone di Budach granted by Grand Master Lascaris to Cesare Passalacqua on the 22 December 1646, unless one accepts the contentions about earlier fiefs.
2 CONT
2 CONT “Motu proprio” means that the relative grants are not be interpreted restrictively. A restrictive interpretation is given where a title of nobility is granted on the request of the grantee (for example a “Rescript”).
2 CONT
2 CONT A Report published in 1878 stated that there were numerous persons descending in the male and female lines who could be lawfully entitled to this title includes persons of all classes, and whilst some live on income from their own
2 CONC  property, others pursue mean occupations and have slender means of support.
2 CONT
2 CONT The correct designation of this title is “Hereditary Noble and Military Armiger of the Holy Roman Empire”. Other published forms of description include “Cavaliere Ereditario”, “Tornearii del Sacro Romano Impero”, “Noble Knight of 
2 CONC the Holy Roman Empire”, “Nobiles Sacri Romani Imperii” and the generic “Noble”. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In Germany and other territories of the Holy Roman Empire, holders of similar titles formed part of the Lower Nobility and were referred to as “Imperial Knights” (German:Reichsritterschaft). 
2 CONT
2 CONT See http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imperial_Knight
2 CONT
