2 CONT
2 CONT Louis de France[1] (1 November 1661 – 14 April 1711) was the eldest son and heir of Louis XIV, King of France and of his spouse, Maria Theresa of Austria. As the heir apparent to the French throne, he was styled as the Dauphin. In
2 CONC  later life he was known as le Grand Dauphin due to his large physical size.
2 CONT
