1 OCCU Duke of Richmond, Earl of March, Baron Settrington, Duke of Lennox, Earl of Darnley and Lord Torbolton, duc d'Aubigny, 1st Duke of Richmond
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Charles [FitzRoy later Lennox], 1st Duke of Richmond, KG PC
2 CONT
2 CONT illegitimate son of King Charles II and his mistress Louise Renée de Penancoet de Kéroualle, suo jure Duchess of Portsmouth and of Aubigny
2 CONT
2 CONT born 29 Jul 1672
2 CONT
2 CONT mar.
2 CONT
2 CONT bef. 10 Jan 1692/3 Lady Anne Belasyse (widow of Henry [Belasyse], 2nd Baron Belasyse;  d. 9 Dec 1722), 3rd dau. of Hon Francis Brudenell, styled Lord Brudenell (by his wife Lady Frances Savile, only dau. by his second wife of Thom
2 CONC as [Savile], 1st Earl of Sussex), son and heir ap. of Robert [Brudenell], 2nd Earl of Cardigan
2 CONT
2 CONT children
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Lord Charles Lennox, later 2nd Duke of Richmond
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Lady Louisa Lennox (b. 24 Dec 1694; d. 15 Jan 1716/7), mar. 13 Feb 1701/2 James [Berkeley], 3rd Earl of Berkeley, and had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Lady Anne Lennox (d. 20 Oct 1789), mar. 21 Feb 1722/3 William Anne [Keppel], 2nd Earl of Albemarle, and has issue
2 CONT
2 CONT died  27 May 1723
2 CONT
2 CONT created
2 CONT
2 CONT 9 Aug 1675 Baron Settrington, of Settrington in the County of York, Earl of March, and Duke of Richmond
2 CONT
2 CONT 9 Sep 1675 Lord Torbolton, Earl of Darnley and Duke of Lennox
2 CONT
2 CONT note
2 CONT
2 CONT received the Castle of Richmond 1675 and the lands of Lennox 1680; Knight of the Garter 1681; Governor of Dumbarton Castle 1681; Master of the Horse 1681-1684/5; High Steward of the City of York 1683; Lord High Admiral 1694; Grand
2 CONC  Master of Freemasons 1696-97; a Lord of the Bedchamber 1714-23; Privy Councillor [I] 1715
2 CONT
2 CONT It appears that he was Master of a Lodge in Chichester in 1696, and so was one of the few known seventeenth century freemasons.
2 CONT
2 CONT ******************************
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipedia: English:  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Lennox,_1st_Duke_of_Richmond
2 CONT
2 CONT Illegitimate son of Charles II king of England
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st Earl of March [England] on 9 August 1675.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st Baron of Settrington, co. York [England] on 9 August 1675.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st Duke of Richmond [England] on 9 August 1675.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st Lord of Torboulton [Scotland] on 9 September 1675.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st Earl of Darnley [Scotland] on 9 September 1675.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st Duke of Lennox [Scotland] on 9 September 1675.
2 CONT
2 CONT In October 1675 he was granted £2,000 per year by his father, as well as a one shilling royalty on every cauldron of coal shipped from Newcastle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Governor of Dumbarton Castle in 1681.
2 CONT
2 CONT Knight, Order of the Garter (K.G.) in 1681.
2 CONT
2 CONT Master of Horse between December 1681 and February 1684/85.
2 CONT
2 CONT High Steward of York in 1683.
2 CONT
2 CONT Naturalized as a French subject, and declared himself Roman Catholic in 1685.
2 CONT
2 CONT Naturalized as a English subject, and converted to the Church of England in 1692.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aide-de-Camp to King William III between 1693 and 1702.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord High Admiral [Scotland] in 1694.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord of the Bedchamber to King George I between 1714 and 1723.
2 CONT
2 CONT Privy Counsellor (P.C.) [Ireland] in 1715.
2 CONT
