2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT From Malford England
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Came in the "James", embarking 6 April and arriving 3 June 1635.  He came with his brother Archelaus as well as his wife and sons Edward and John and had 4 more children born here.  Freeman 25 May 1636.  Licensed to sell wine and 
2 CONC strong water.  Deputy, Town Officer.  Active in church agitation.  He was a wealthy and prominent man.  Was lieutenant in a company sent against Pequods in April 1637.
2 CONT
2 CONT National Society Daughters of Colonial Wars, 1950; "Lieut. of the Newbury Company, 1637.  Served in the Pequot War, 1637.  Dep to the General Court from Newbury 1636, 37, 39."
