1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From the Mellott-Eastman family tree:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.reidmellott.com/Genealogy/getperson.php?personID=P3281741182&tree=metree
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham Merlette
2 CONT *Birth  26 Jan 1656  Long Island, Kings, New York, USA
2 CONT **(This is in error, as the Merlet family would not be in the New World for another 6 years.)
2 CONT *Gender  Male  
2 CONT *Died  1 Jun 1714  Pisacataway, Middlesex, New Jersey, USA  
2 CONT *Person ID  P3281741182  
2 CONT **Mellott - Eastman Family Tree 
2 CONT **Last Modified  20 May 2009  
2 CONT *Father  Gedeon La Plante Merlet,   
2 CONT **b. Feb 1624, Champagne, Dordogne, Aquitaine, France ,   
2 CONT **d. Feb 1683, Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey, USA  
2 CONT *Mother  Margaret Martin,   
2 CONT **b. 1622, Limbourg, Liege, Belgium ,   
2 CONT **d. 25 Aug 1681, Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey, USA   
2 CONT *Married  21 Aug 1644  
2 CONT **Walloon Church, Leiden, Zuid-Holland, Netherlands  
2 CONT *Family ID  F47  Group Sheet 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources  
2 CONT *1.[S3585957191] Ancestry Family Trees, (Online publication - Provo, UT, USA: The Generations Network. Original data: Family Tree files submitted by Ancestry members.), Ancestry Family Trees.
2 CONT ** http://trees.ancestry.com/pt/AMTCitationRedir.aspx?tid=7873509&pid=-1013226114
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT From the page of his father in the Mellott-Eastman family tree:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.reidmellott.com/Genealogy/getperson.php?personID=P3281738676&tree=metree
2 CONT
2 CONT After living in Leyden from about 1643 until the 1650's, Gedeon, Marguerite and the first three children moved to Mannheim, in the German Palatinate, an area known as a haven for French Huguenots at that time. There two more sons 
2 CONC were born and baptized, namely Abraham and Jean Pierre MERLET, MERLETTE, MARLETTE or MARLET.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the records of the French Huguenot Church of Mannheim, Germany: "On February 7, 1656, was baptized in the Church of Mannheim, Merlette, Abraham, son of Gedeon and Marguerite Martin."
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT From SHIP PASSENGER LISTS: NEW YORK AND NEW JERSEY (1600-1825), edited and indexed by Carl Boyer, 3rd (Self-Published: Newhall, CA, 1978), p. 130.
2 CONT
2 CONT "October 12, 1662. In De Purmerlander Kerck Gedeon Merlitt, wife and four children, 15, 8, 6, and 4 years old." [The four sons were Josue or Josias; Poulus or Paul; Jean Pierre or John Peter; Abraham.]
2 CONT
2 CONT The following is an address made by C. L. Marlatt on Oct. 27, 1935 on behalf of the Huguenot Memorial Association on the occasion of the 250th Anniversary of the Edict of Nantes. The address took place at the Memorial Church of th
2 CONC e Huguenots at Huguenot Park, Staten Island, New York. "Two additional Huguenot immigrants have recently been honored by having their names recorded in this edifice, namely Gedeon Merlet and his youngest son, Abraham." ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Gedeon's youngest son, Abraham, married about 1677 Christence Billieu, daughter of Pierre Billieu - a Huguenot immigrant of 1661 and prominent in the early settlement of Staten Island. Two children came from this union, viz., Marg
2 CONC aret, baptized March 31, 1678, and Abraham, May 16, 1680.
2 CONT
2 CONT We have little information as to Abraham, the youngest son of Gedeon, except that he was for a period collector for the southern part of Staten Island.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Mr. C. L. Marlatt, who delivered the above address, referred to his ancestor, Abraham Merlet as "the youngest child" of Gedeon's family. Perhaps in 1935 the baptismal certificate of Jean Pierre Merlet had not yet been found at th
2 CONC e French Huguenot of Mannheim, in the Palatinate region of Germany. The baptismal record of Jean Pierre Merlet (born 1658) indicates he was born after Abraham Merlet (born 1656).]
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT From Bill Marlatt's Gedeon Merlett Family Tree:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.malott.net/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=40&Itemid=54#i33
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham [2] Marlett (Gedeon [1] Merlet) was born in Mannheim, Baden, Germany 1656. 
2 CONT *He married Christience Billeau in Staten Island, NY, 1678. 
2 CONT *Abraham Marlett and Christience Billeau had the following child: 
2 CONT **1. Abraham [3] Marlatt was born 16 May 1680. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Christening: 2 FEB 1655/56 Huguenot Church, Mannheim, Palatinate, GERMANY
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham is believed to have been married twice during his life.  He married first in about 1677 in New York to Christence Billieu.  Christence, who was listed in at least one Staten Island record as "Corten Billieu", was the daugh
2 CONC ter of Peter Billieu.  According to available records, on 17 mar 1678, Abraham Marlet was given one half of a lot of land on Staten Island by his brother Paulus.  This lot was apparently being received by Paulus out of his father'
2 CONC s land patent.  Other records indicate that Abraham was elected in 1698 and again in 1703, to be the Tax Collector for the South Division of Staten Island.  Sometime after his first wife passed away, Abraham married for a second t
2 CONC ime to a woman named Elizabeth.  Although a number of researchers believe her to be Elizabeth Morgan, this has not been substantiated.  After their marriage, Abraham and Elizabeth settled at Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey. Abra
2 CONC ham died at Piscataway in 1716.  His will, which was dated 6June 1714, was subsequently probated before the Middlesex County Court on 16 May 1716.
2 CONT --------------------
