0 @N6000000001956329166@ NOTE
1 CONT It is interesting that Henri Bourbon, ruled as King Henri III of Navarre (a land to the south west of France), at the same time that Henri Valois ruled France, as King Henri III of France. When Henri III of France was assassinated
1 CONC , Henri III of Navarre also became Henri IV of France. 
1 CONT Despite Henri of Navarre's apparent distance from the Valois line, he was in fact closely related to them, through his mother's line.
1 CONT His maternal grandmother was Marguerite of Angouleme, sister of the Valois King Francois I (Born 1494, King 1516, Died 1547). They were the children of Charles of Orleans, Count of Angouleme and Louise of Savoy.
1 CONT Marguerite of Angouleme married Henri II of Albret, King of Navarre and their daughter, Jeanne D'Albret, became Queen of Navarre, before passing the throne of Navarre onto her son Henri III of Navarre. 
1 CONT It was the son of the Valois King Francois I, King Henri II of France, who with Catherine de Medici, begat the French Kings, King Francois II, King Charles IX, King Henri III and Marguerite Valois, first wife of Henri III of Navar
1 CONC re. 
1 CONT Despite the endorsement of Henri III of France, many people would not accept a Protestant as their King, and Henri of Navarre had to continue to do battle with the Catholic league, who received strong support from Spain.
1 CONT On the 25th of July 1593, Henri III of Navarre converted back to the Catholic faith, which led to him being officially crowned as Henri IV of France at Chartres, on the 27th of February 1594.
