0 @N6000000002322342859@ NOTE By the treaty of Arras in 1482, Maximilian I, father of Margaret, was forced
1 CONT to consent to the bethrothal of his daughter (Margaret) to Charles VIII of
1 CONT France. In 1486, Maximilian, in order to surround France, married Duchess
1 CONT Anne of Brittany by proxy, but he could not forestall an invasion of Brittany
1 CONT by France. A dramatic setback occurred when Charles VIII sent his finacee
1 CONT Margaret back to her father, Maximilian, and required Anne of Brittany to
1 CONT severe her marriage to Maximilian and to become the queen of France.
