0 @N6000000005598767786@ NOTE Every great family worth tabloid-bashing has had a curse, andthe Hapsburggirls and boys were no exception.  The only dynastyto rule for twentygenerations without ever having had an actualcountry, the Hapsburgs'power began with a s
1 CONC mall dukedom inAustria and spread like crabgrassacross Europe via marriage.The original curse was prtty meager --something about apregnant peasant girl and a randy Hapsburg teen.  Butthe 'true'family curse was The Lip (in point of
1 CONC  fact, the entirejaw).Populations of good-sized cities could have taken shelter underaHapsburg chin.  Wobbly and red as a cherry Jell-O, The Lipmade many malesof the family look moronic.  So you an justimagine how Princess Anna of
1 CONC Austria and all the other HapsburgAnnas, Marys, Elizabeths, andChrisintes felt when they lookedin a mirror.Among other thankless tasts,Anna married King Louis XIII,producd a Louie heir, and ran France asqueen regent from 1643to 16
1 CONC 61.  Spanish-born Anna brought new ideas tothe Frenchcourt.  Naturally they all tittered when she first lifted acupof some dirty brown substance to those Austria-sized lips.  ButAnnapersisted jutting out a chin that would stun Jay
1 CONC  Leno intosilence.  Thedrink she introduced -- hot chocolate --eventually becme the onlybeverage fit for the Beautiful Peopleto quaff, once she got ht ehang ofadding sugar to it.  Forages, the drink was deemed to be an aphrodisiac
1 CONC in the bargain.Ole! for Queen of Chocolate Anna, who gave owmen of theworldthe serotonin-loaded solace they so desperately needed.
