1 CONT Charles I Stuart, King of Great Britain was the son of James I Charles Stuart, King of Great Britain <p10137.htm> and Anne Oldenburg, Princess of Denmark. He was born on 19 November 1600 at Dunfermline Palace, Dunfermline, Fife, S
1 CONC cotland.1 He was baptised on 23 December 1600.1 He married Henrietta Maria de Bourbon <p10139.htm>, daughter of Henri IV, Roi de France <p10139.htm> and Marie de Medici <p10139.htm>, on 13 June 1625 at St. Augustine's Church, Cant
1 CONC erbury, Kent, England, Married by proxy earlier, on 1 May, in Paris.2 He died on 30 January 1649 at age 48 at Whitehall Palace, Whitehall, London, England, by a public beheading.3 He was buried on 7 February 1649 at Henry VIII vau
1 CONC lt, Windsor, Berkshire, England.  He was created 1st Earl of Ross [Scotland] on 23 December 1600.1 He was created 1st Lord Ardmannoch [Scotland] on 23 December 1600.1 He was created 1st Marquess of Ormond [Scotland] on 23 December
1 CONC  1600.1 He was created 1st Duke of Albany [Scotland] on 23 December 1600.1 He was created 1st Duke of York [England] on 6 January 1605.4 He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Garter (K.G.) on 24 April 1611.2 He succeeded to th
1 CONC e title of Duke of Rothesay on 6 November 1612.1 He succeeded to the title of Duke of Cornwall on 6 November 1612.2 He was created 1st Earl of Chester [England] on 4 November 1616.2 He was created Prince Charles of Wales on 4 Nove
1 CONC mber 1616.2 He succeeded to the title of King Charles I of Great Britain on 27 March 1625.5 He was crowned King of England, Scotland, France and Ireland, Defender of the Faith on 2 February 1626 at Westminster Abbey, Westminster, 
1 CONC London, England.5 He was deposed as King of Great Britain on 27 January 1649.5 He has an extensive biography in the Dictionary of National Biography.6  <e76.htm> <e76.htm>
