0 @N6000000002176664561@ NOTE During her life, the war, bubonic plague, slave raids, and mass murders had
1 CONT reduced the total population of Poland to approximately 4 million people, or
1 CONT 45% of the former total population, The cities suffered worst of all, losing
1 CONT all manufacturing establishments and industrial enterprises along with
1 CONT three-quarters of all their inhabitants. The tremendous costs of war caused
1 CONT the greatest inflation in Polish history. The war, conducted in the spirit of
1 CONT religious struggles, deleted the constitutional maxim of religious tolerance.
